From 1dfbfc9f8c61dee9cdd83634149e2be61dccbfd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Solis <k9track@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 1 May 2026 11:34:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Garmin background staleness + barcode serving-size
 accuracy

GarminManager: subscribe to UIApplication foreground/active notifications
and trigger a fresh watch push on resume. While Trio is suspended its
publishers stop firing and ConnectIQ delivery is gated, so the watch went
stale until the user manually relaunched the app. Clears lastSentDataHash
on resume so dedup can't suppress the first push.

FoodDatabaseService: prefer OpenFoodFacts' structured serving_quantity
field over the free-text serving_size string (which often contains the
package weight rather than a serving). Suspiciously large values (>250g)
are dropped so the UI defaults to 100g for the user to adjust. Adds
os_log diagnostics on every lookup. Removes dead duplicate
EditServingSizeView.swift that wasn't in the xcode project and didn't
compile against the current FoodItem type.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
